   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "Cameron-Gallegos Medical Group\nRe: Bethany Collins (DOB 01/03/1968)\n\nSeptember 14, 2024\nBethany Collins visited the clinic today for follow-up regarding her prediabetes, which includes impaired fasting glucose. Her blood pressure was 136/85, and her weight was 162 pounds. Bethany has been managing her condition with metformin 850 mg. Her most recent A1c level was 5.8, showing good control overall.\n\nFebruary 16, 2024\nBethany returned to the clinic with symptoms of a URI. Her blood pressure was 134/86, and her weight was 177 pounds. Despite the recent illness, Bethany continues to manage her prediabetes effectively. Her A1c level remains steady at 5.9.\n\nJuly 19, 2023\nBethany was seen for ongoing management of her prediabetes. Her blood pressure 123/90, and her weight was 170 pounds. She is doing well and adhering to her medication regimen of metformin 850 mg.\n\nDecember 20, 2022\nBethany visited for routine monitoring of her prediabetes. Her blood pressure was 126/87, and her weight was 176 pounds. She has been stable, and her A1c level was 6. This is slightly elevated but manageable with her current treatment plan.\n\nMay 22, 2022\nBethany came in for her annual flu shot. Her blood pressure was 126/87, and her weight was 176 pounds. She is doing well with her prediabetes well managed and her A1c level at 5.9.\n\nOctober 23, 2021\nBethany's annual physical exam was conducted. Her blood pressure was 139/89, and her weight was 178 pounds. Overall, she is in good health, and her prediabetes is under control with her current medication, metformin 850 mg.\n\nMarch 25, 2021\nBethany visited for her flu shot. Her blood pressure was 128/88, and her weight was 170 pounds. She continues to manage her prediabetes well, with an A1c level of 5.7.\n\nBethany's A1c trend over the years is as follows:\n- September 24, 2024: 5.8\n- February 24, 2024: 5.9\n- July 23, 2023: S.9\n- December 22, 2022: 6\n\nSocial History:\nBethany is a former smoker who quit in September 2022. She used to smoke half a pack per day, starting in December 2002. Additionally, she consumes approximately three alcoholic drinks per week.\n\nAttached Lab Results from Heritage Diagnostic Services (06/28/12):\n- Cholesterol/HDL: 298/56\n- Fructosamine: 241\n- Nicotine Metabolite: Negative\n- Gamma GT: 52\n\nDr. Ashlee Peterson\nCameron-Gallegos Medical Group\nEndocrinology\n"
