   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "[FAX] p.1 ---- Ross PLC Clinic\n\npt Collins dob 01/03/68\n04/18 - Prediabetes impaired fasting glucose bp 139/84 wt 168 f/u 3mo\n04/10 - URI bp 129/90 wt 169 ok\n04/02 - Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose bp 129/88 wt 166 cont meds\n\nDx: Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose (A1c 5.7)\n\nA1C trend: 04/25 5.8, 04/24 5.6, 04/23 5.9\n\nSocial: tobacco - cigarette former 1/2 ppd, quit 2022-09\nSocial: alcohol ~3 drinks/week\n\nProvider: Dr. Jenny Elliott, family medicine\n\n[FAX] p.2\n\nMs. Collins is a 57 y/o female pt who presented for routine f/u of prediabetes. Pt reports good compliance with metformin 850 mg. No recent episodes of hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia noted. Continues to have stable levels.\n\nReview of Systems:\nConstitutional: Denies weight loss, fatigue, fever, or chills. Reports stable energy levels.\nHEENT: Denies headaches, dizziness, or changes in vision. No ear pain, sore throat, or nasal congestion.\nCardiovascular: Denies chest pain, palpitations, or shortness of breath.\nRespiratory: Denies cough, wheezing, or difficulty breathing.\nGI: Denies nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, or constipation. Reports normal appetite.\nGU: Denies dysuria, hematuria, or urinary frequency.\nMusculoskeletal: Denies muscle pain, joint pain, or stiffness.\nNeurological: Denies numbness, tingling, or weakness.\nPsychiatric: Denies depression, anxiety, mood changes.\nSkin: Denies rashes, lesions, or changes in skin color.\n\nPhysical Exam:\nVS: BP 13g/84, HR 72, RR 16, Temp 98.6F, Wt 168 lbs\nGeneral: Alert, oriented, no acute distress\nHEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic. Pupils equal, round, reactive to light. TMs intact. Oropharynx clear.\nNeck: Supple, no lymphadenopathy\nCardiovascular: RRR, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops\nRespiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi\nAbdomen: Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly\nExtremities: No edema, good pulses\nNeurological: CN II-XII intact, normal motor and sensory exam\n\nLabs:\nA1C 04/18/25: 5.8\nA1C 04/10/24: 5.6\nA1C 04/02/23: 5.9\n\n[FAX] p.3\n\nAssessment:\n1. Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose - Controlled. Pt continues to manage condition well with metformin 850 mg. A1C levels remain stable.\n\nPlan:\n1. Continue current regimen of metformin 850 mg. F/u in 3 months for re-evaluation.\n2. Encourage continued healthy lifestyle modifications including diet and exercise.\n3. Review importance of regular monitoring and adherence to medication.\n4. Discuss potential risks associated with prediabetes and importance of prevention strategies.\n\nSocial History:\nPt reports former tobacco use, 1/2 ppd cigarettes, quit in 2022"
